LIVE AND REPLAY MODES\
\
Every API-calling command requires explicit --mode live.\
Do not default to live mode.\
\
Replay:\
- Uses deterministic teaching fixtures.\
- Requires no credentials or network.\
- Clearly identifies fixtures as authored teaching examples.\
- Does not pretend to be a live observation.\
- Does not invent measured API latency or token usage.\
- Must not validate a judge by reading expected labels and returning\
  those labels as if independently produced.\
- Uses separate fixture outputs, which can be compared with labels.\
- Must not force Prompt B to win.\
\
Fixed replay outputs cannot demonstrate live-model variation.\
Repeated replay runs are only a workflow demonstration.\
\
Live:\
- Uses configured model IDs and supported SDK interfaces.\
- Records the actual returned model ID when available.\
- Uses bounded retries for transient errors only.\
- Counts retry attempts and disables conflicting SDK retry behaviour\
  where needed to keep the total bounded.\
- Preserves errors.\
- Never switches silently to replay after a live failure.\
- Never retries merely because an answer received a low score.\
